-- #118 완전 담보 계약과 주문 잠금 (ADR-0107 결정 1 #177 3·7항, 결정 2 #73 1항, 결정 3 (2); ADR-0110).
-- Generated by `drizzle-kit generate`, then hand-edited where marked: this header only. The
-- snapshot is as generated.
--
-- - positions.locked_qty: the contracts of a holding that live sell orders hold (매도 주문의 수량
--   잠금), 0 to `qty` by `positions_locked_qty_check`. Only `qty - locked_qty` can be locked again,
--   burned or sold (@buddha/db contracts.ts); a trade fill takes both down together; settlement's
--   qty-0 UPDATE fails on a row still locked, so a market with a live sell stays SETTLING.
--
-- No row is deleted or rewritten, so this migration waits on no owner (결정 3 (2)): the column's
-- constant default makes the ADD COLUMN a catalog-only change (PostgreSQL 11 and later), and the
-- CHECK holds for every row already there (0 <= 0 <= qty, `positions_qty_check` keeps qty >= 0);
-- the deployed `positions` is empty since 0060's wipe anyway. No wipe, no grant (buddha_app
-- already writes every column of `positions`), no function and no trigger. A Coin lock needs no
-- column: it moves `balances.available_coin` to `locked_coin` of one account, no ledger event.
ALTER TABLE "positions" ADD COLUMN "locked_qty" integer DEFAULT 0 NOT NULL;--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TABLE "positions" ADD CONSTRAINT "positions_locked_qty_check" CHECK ("positions"."locked_qty" >= 0 AND "positions"."locked_qty" <= "positions"."qty");